      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two cases are presented in which a half Palmaz-Schatz stent was implanted in a short lesion located in the ostium of a saphenous vein graft. Aorto-ostial stenoses are a technical challenge for balloon angioplasty and stenting. Short stents may offer several advantages as regards deployment, positioning, thrombogenicity, and restenosis."},
